# The two superblock totals.  Zeroed here, so both are wrong and neither is a plausible
# accident -- fsck must recompute each from its own walk and offer a FIX, and the host's
# checker must fault the image before and pass it afterwards like any other repair.
#
# This was the tree's one `hostblind' case, back when nothing maintained the two fields and
# fsck could only note them.  kernel/alloc.c maintains both now; see cmd/fsck/README.md SS1.
sb.tfree=0
sb.tinode=0
